PKA Solver
Copyright (c) 2026 Raka Syauqi Ferdian

This software is a Python port of the Cisco Packet Tracer .pka decryption
logic from pka2xml:

    pka2xml
    https://github.com/mircodz/pka2xml
    Copyright (c) 2020 Mirco De Zorzi
    Licensed under the BSD 2-Clause License (see LICENSE)

The port covers the Twofish-128 + EAX construction, the two XOR obfuscation
passes, the length-prefixed zlib stream, and the on-disk layout of the
`<PACKETTRACER5>` blocks. The decryption logic is reimplemented in Python and
extended with the answer-key reader, the rubric extractor, the block-transplant
solver, the tool and UI surfaces, and the bundled pure-Python Twofish cipher.

Third-party components
----------------------

Twofish
    Algorithm by Bruce Schneier et al. The pure-Python implementation in
    twofish_pure.py follows the Gladman byte-oriented reference structure and
    is validated against the published known-answer vectors (Twofish book,
    appendix B.2) and against the loxodo implementation
    (https://github.com/sommer/loxodo).

pycryptodome (test-only, optional)
    Used in selftest.py as an independent AES-EAX oracle for cross-checking the
    hand-written EAX mode. Not required at runtime.

